        "id": 59401,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-11T15:50:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>So a 2 player game isn't highly encouraged.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nMinor clarification: A two <em>hero</em> game isn't supported/encouraged (but it doesn't mean you can't play it&nbsp; :wink:  ). A two <em>player</em> game is supported, with the recommendation of using two heroes each, or at least one player using two heroes.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>True. Funny how&nbsp;I referred to 3-5 as heroes but whenever I typed 2 I followed it with players. You would think I would be better at that since I play 1 player all the time, but I also play 3 hero games at the same time.</p>",
